  "enisaUuid": "5e8d4628-a20c-32b3-9b14-1924ccf298d2",
  "description": "A Improper Input Validation issue affecting the v2_sdk_service running on a set of DJI drone devices on the port 10000 could allow an attacker to cause a crash of the service through a crafted payload triggering a missing input size check in the process_push_file function implemented in the libv2_sdk.so library used by the dji_vtwo_sdk binary implementing the service, compromising it in a term of availability and producing a denial-of-service attack. Affected models are Mavic 3 Pro until v01.01.0300, Mavic 3 until v01.00.1200, Mavic 3 Classic until v01.00.0500, Mavic 3 Enterprise until v07.01.10.03, Matrice 300 until v57.00.01.00, Matrice M30 until v07.01.0022 and Mini 3 Pro until v01.00.0620.",
